     I've considered implementing this in the past, but never gotten
around to doing so.  One feasible implementation is trivial; testing to
see whether it has any impact on game play is more work:  when adding
a monster's next allotment of movement points, just tack on something
like ``+ rn2(2) - rn2(2)'' and it will then have the chance to vary by
plus or minus one unit over the monster's usual amount.  No extra fields
or counters; just rely on the RNG to even things out.  Of course plus or
minus one might not be big enough when the base rate is 12 units, and
dismally slow monsters probably end up needing a little extra handling.


